{#- Atlas — surface one: project depth on a desk (decisions 22, 23, 24, 25).

  Workstreams are columns; one shared ladder runs down (decision 20). Three pre-milestone stages
  sit above the first milestone (decision 23). For each column the bar covers what is complete and
  the arrowhead points at what is next (decision 24), and the tip carries the reason the column
  stopped there (decision 25).

  Both ends of every column come from `computeLadder`. This template positions nothing of its own:
  it looks up which ladder row `barTo` and `headAt` name and paints those. The arrowhead sits one
  row past the bar and never on it — an off-by-one that was a real bug in the mockups — and
  `computeLadder` is what guarantees it.

  Data this layout expects:
    ladder      — { rows, columns } exactly as computeLadder returned it
    workstreams — the array resolveWorkstreams produced, in the SAME order as ladder.columns, so
                  ladder.columns[i] describes workstreams[i]
    project, repo, title — see base.njk
-#}
{% extends "base.njk" %}
{% import "base.njk" as ui %}

{% block bodyClass %}page page-depth{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<h1>Project depth</h1>
<p class="lede">One ladder down, a column for each workstream. The bar covers what is complete; the head points at what is next, and says why the column stopped there.</p>

<div class="chart-scroll" role="region" aria-labelledby="depth-caption" tabindex="0">
<table class="depth-chart">
<caption id="depth-caption">Every workstream against one shared ladder. Rows above the numbers are the stages a workstream passes through before its first milestone.</caption>
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col" class="ladder-head">Ladder</th>
{% for column in ladder.columns %}
<th scope="col" class="column-head" data-column="{{ column.codename }}">
<a href="/workstream/{{ workstreams[loop.index0].slug }}/">{{ column.codename }}</a>
{{ ui.chip("stage", column.stage) }}
</th>
{% endfor %}
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{% for row in ladder.rows %}
{%- set rowIndex = loop.index0 %}
<tr data-rowkind="{{ row.kind }}">
<th scope="row" class="ladder-cell">{% if row.kind == "milestone" %}<span class="num">{{ row.label }}</span>{% else %}{{ row.label }}{% endif %}</th>
{% for column in ladder.columns -%}
{%- set stream = workstreams[loop.index0] -%}
{#- Where this column's bar ends and where its head sits, looked up by the row ids computeLadder
    named. Nothing here recomputes a position. -#}
{%- set barIndex = -1 -%}
{%- set headIndex = -1 -%}
{%- for candidate in ladder.rows -%}
{%- if candidate.id == column.barTo %}{% set barIndex = loop.index0 %}{% endif -%}
{%- if candidate.id == column.headAt %}{% set headIndex = loop.index0 %}{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set state = "beyond" -%}
{%- if rowIndex == headIndex %}{% set state = "head" %}{% elif rowIndex <= barIndex %}{% set state = "covered" %}{% endif -%}
{#- This column's own milestone at this depth, if it has one: decision 20 means each column shows
    its own ids rather than the ladder's row number. -#}
{%- set cellLabel = "" -%}
{%- set cellStatus = "" -%}
{%- if row.depth -%}
{%- for entry in stream.manifest.milestones -%}
{%- if entry.depth == row.depth %}{% set cellLabel = entry.label %}{% set cellStatus = entry.status %}{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif %}
<td class="cell cell-{{ state }}" data-row="{{ row.id }}" data-column="{{ column.codename }}" data-state="{{ state }}">
{%- if state == "head" -%}
<span class="head-mark" aria-hidden="true">&#9660;</span><span class="head-next">Next up</span><span class="cell-label num">{{ column.tipLabel }}</span>{% if cellStatus %}{{ ui.chip("status", cellStatus) }}{% else %}<span class="cell-state">Not on record yet</span>{% endif %}<p class="tip-note">{{ column.note }}</p>
{%- elif cellLabel -%}
<span class="cell-label num">{{ cellLabel }}</span>{{ ui.chip("status", cellStatus) }}
{%- elif state == "covered" -%}
<span class="cell-state">Passed</span>
{%- endif -%}
</td>
{% endfor %}
</tr>
{%- endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endblock %}
